  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Liberia: Strengthening TIP Response in the Justice and Security Sectors</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Direct beneficiaries: Liberia National Police (LNP), Liberia Immigration Service                (LIS), Liberia Drugs Enforcement Agency (LDEA), Judiciary (Judicial Institute, judges, magistrates and                public defenders), Ministry of Justice (prosecutors and city solicitors), Ministry of Labour, National                Anti-Trafficking Task Force (NATT), Liberia Female Law Enforcement Agency. Indirect beneficiaries:                Survivors or trafficking in persons (TIP) and residents of Liberia at risk of TIP.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project aimed to combat trafficking in persons (TIP) in all its forms in                Liberia</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">To enhance the capacity of law enforcement and justice actors to investigate,                prosecute and adjudicate TIP.</narrative>
  </description>
